y  circumstances not because the element is  dangerous on its own but because of the  potential it holds in other people's  hands now as she says this the scene  cuts to another scene that takes place  in a wakandan research center we see a  group of people with guns infiltrate the  facility in search of vibranium tools  they find a vibranium covered wall and  markings and when they get to it and  activate it the markings light up  meanwhile it cuts back to the queen  saying at the un you perform civility  here but we know what you whisper in  your halls of leadership and in your  military facilities the king is dead the  black panther is gone they have lost  their protectors now while she's saying  this it keeps cutting back and forth  between that scene on the research  center but the dora milaje appears and  actually one of the dora malaji was  undercover disguised as a research  assistant it then shows the dora malaji  led by okoye going off against the  mercenaries who broke into the research  facility and as queen raimondo's talking  comes to an end we actually see the dora  milaje enter the assembly with the  mercenaries that they have defeated from  here the trailer showed old shots from  the first trailer it includes a glowing  sunset of wakanda and t'challa's funeral  and then we get more footage in this  time of namor it appears that queen  raimonda and namor are actually meeting  with each other however umbaku quickly  attacks neymar with the staff which  immediately smashes to pieces and when  embaku actually hits neymar namor  doesn't even react to the attack so for  those who were wondering if namor is  going to be big bad and strong the  answer is yes but the trailer ends with  an explosion on a city bridge and it  ends with a shot of the new black  panther and the final line that says  show them who we are and that was the  exclusive clip trailer that was shown at  d23 this past saturday now there are  some very important things to break down  here 